{
  "slug": "artist:chief-keef",
  "name": "Chief Keef",
  "editorial_article": "Born Keith Farrelle Cozart in Chicago in 1995, Chief Keef is a rapper and record producer who defined the drill subgenre. He gained early attention through YouTube videos filmed while under house arrest in 2011, eventually signing a deal with Interscope Records. His debut album 'Finally Rich' (2012) featured the hit 'I Don't Like,' which drew a remix from Kanye West, Pusha T, Jadakiss, and Big Sean. In 2013, he contributed a vocal hook to 'Hold My Liquor' on West's 'Yeezus' album. Following his departure from Interscope in 2014, he founded the label Glo Gang, serving as a primary producer for mixtapes like 'Back from the Dead 2.' His 2024 album 'Almighty So 2' followed a years-long path of independent releases, often featuring self-produced beats and collaborations with artists such as Zaytoven.",
